<p>Notes: (a) Excluding non-recurring special charge associated with the payment of a bonus to Parris Holmes Jr upon his resigination as chairman of the company on June 2, 1997. The charge, totalling $1.2 million or $734,000 after tax, includes a cash bonus of $875,000 and the value of 25,000 shares of restricted common stock were granted to him. Including this non-recurring special charge, the company had a net income of $1.1 million or $0.07 per share for the third quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>(b) EBITDA is a profitability/cash flow measurement that is commonly used in the telecommunications industry.</p>
<p>In order to reflect the operating results of the company on a stand-alone basis, these consolidated pro forma statements of operations exclude direct spin-off costs involving completion the spinoff of the company's Billing Information Concepts Corp on August 2, 1996. Direct spin-off costs were $6.6 million for the three-month period ended June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>Full company name is U.S. Long Distance Corp.</p>
